      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "Just switching imports doesn't work - you'd have to modify the code.  The reason we're seeing this error, I believe, is that simply adding adam_atan2 from PyPI via PIP is not resulting in the building of the CUDA module adam_atan2_backend, which is missing because it needs to be compiled.  \n\nIt would be useful if the Sapient folks could clarify this step in the installation process.  ",
